@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] firecracker-pci-bar-relocation
The patched virtio PCI transport MUST allocate the MSI-X table and PBA in a
dedicated BAR whose address is tracked independently from the queue BAR. A
64-bit BAR relocation MUST take effect only after its high-half write, and
queue ioevents MUST be moved only after the complete relocation succeeds. A
device removal MUST unregister both BARs and all queue ioevents; a failed or
partial relocation MUST leave the prior registration usable.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;recovery] firecracker-native-queue-init
Virtio queue size and address writes made while a native illumos guest is
initializing with device status zero MUST be accepted when they form a valid
queue configuration. Invalid queue indices, sizes, addresses or writes after
the device has entered a disallowed state MUST retain the existing refusal and
MUST NOT create ioevents or expose an unconfigured queue.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;recovery] firecracker-pci-config-notification
Virtio queue notifications through the PCI configuration access capability MUST
signal the same queue event as its MMIO doorbell. Only 16-bit or 32-bit writes
whose queue value matches the aligned notification offset and an existing queue
MAY signal an event. Malformed writes MUST leave every queue event untouched.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;recovery] firecracker-msix-reset-state
The guest-visible MSI-X Enable and Function Mask bits MUST reset to zero and
match the internal disabled/unmasked state. Individual vector entries MUST
remain masked until programmed. Queue interrupts MUST NOT inject while MSI-X
is disabled; a guest's conditional enable write MUST activate the same state
used to route subsequent interrupts.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:isolation;recovery] firecracker-net-reset-allocation
Network reset in a vCPU thread MUST discard abandoned ring references while
retaining the preallocated receive mapping. Reset MUST NOT require memfd_create
or broaden the existing seccomp filter to allocate replacement buffers.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;recovery] firecracker-uart-thre-enable
Enabling UART transmit-empty interrupts while THR is empty MUST set the pending
THRE identification and signal its interrupt, including re-enabling an existing
pending interrupt. An unchanged enable bit MUST NOT signal again. DLAB divisor
writes MUST NOT change interrupt enable or emit this interrupt.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;recovery] firecracker-cloudhv-poweroff
The fixed CloudHv firmware port 0x600 MUST signal the existing VMM exit event
only for a single-byte value 0x34 at offset zero. Reads, malformed writes and other
values MUST remain inert. Native clean-shutdown evidence MUST require the real
guest to sync and power off with VMM exit zero; timeout termination cannot count.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;recovery] firecracker-omnios-serial-shutdown
The x86 serial output path MUST signal the existing VMM exit event only after the exact contiguous OmniOS filesystem-sync marker has been written, preserve bounded partial matches across output calls, and retain no guest output bytes in diagnostics.
